#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096351 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "87747005-ce77-5ec6-9f44-af074633aa98" :question/math-academy-id "e-401" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=4-x^2$ between $x=-1,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown below. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/assets/b517da6e730ac50341b133a60ae8ab99cfed7b2ce92638e6028bb3fac6fbf9da.png)" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} f(x_k)\\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_k = a + k\\Delta x$ with $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=2,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{2-(-1)}{3} = \\dfrac 3 3 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+kΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3-1}f(-1+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}f(k-1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(4-(k-1)^{2}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(4-{k}^{2}+2k-1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(3+2k-{k}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096352 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "af666c8f-dfb7-548e-a8f1-1922d4c2fdc5" :question/math-academy-id "e-402" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{ x}{2}\\right)$ between $x=0$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $3$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^n f(x_i)\\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_i = a + i\\Delta x$ and $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nNote that here we are using the index $i$ instead of $k.$ It doesn't matter which letter we use for the counter.\n\nWe're told that there are $n=3$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{3-0}{3} = \\dfrac{3}{3} = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}f(0+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}f(i) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{i}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9c21429-afef-5da0-8202-11be6ddd791c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6j}{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9c21429-afef-5da0-8202-11be6ddd791c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6j}{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385360} :answer-field/id #uuid "14892792-cc54-5740-9310-398085dbf81d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "18d22bab-9d00-5b28-aee4-2073bc2ebbb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-315701" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-4)$ between $x=2$ and $x=5$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{3}{n}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡($\n\n{{field-1}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of subintervals, ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$, and  $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nThe endpoints indicate that $a=2$ and $b=5,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-2}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(2+j\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{3}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(2+\\frac{3j}{n})-4) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6j}{n}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54cbbc91-f971-50d1-bdfe-f67d7a062db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{j}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54cbbc91-f971-50d1-bdfe-f67d7a062db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{j}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385363} :answer-field/id #uuid "e55005cf-fd3c-5c5a-b364-407394b9b86a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2728f5cf-d423-5d6d-b117-9f0f9c4bc61a" :question/math-academy-id "q-315717" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=(x+2)^{3/2}$ between $x=-2$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $10$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j.$*\n\n${S}_{L}=\\frac{1}{2}$\n ${\\sum }_{j=0}^{9}($\n{{field-1}}$)^{3/2}$" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're given that there are  $n=10$ subintervals.  The endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=3,$  so the step size is \n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-2)}{10}=\\frac{5}{10}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{10-1}f(-2+j\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{9}f(\\frac{2j-4}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{9}{((-2+\\frac{j}{2})+2)}^{3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{9}{(\\frac{j}{2})}^{3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dac1881b-9d38-5d55-b403-c105260f9981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{1+k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385366} {:answer/id #uuid "76ce1408-4b6f-5f98-9970-8dbe17c284aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{2+k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dac1881b-9d38-5d55-b403-c105260f9981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{1+k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385366} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fc3d5df-590b-554b-9fad-df5140078067" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fe864c7b-9ad1-5abf-a889-bb7b2a7a7382" :question/math-academy-id "q-345027" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/assets/e81e7d9d60e38c52f86c5eee784ebcfdeb91d4445b6539cc01a6ac9f5ededa89.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\frac{6}{x}$ between $x=1$, $x=6$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $k.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=5$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=6,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{6-1}{5}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+kΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{5-1}f(1+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4}f(1+k) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4}\\frac{6}{1+k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf67984-9161-531b-890f-2c4c46ebcde5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20j}{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260057} {:answer/id #uuid "2f1d3e07-4c12-5426-91d7-f9501aa9d9c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20j}{n}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bf67984-9161-531b-890f-2c4c46ebcde5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20j}{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260057} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6d39e5-5a0a-5535-9436-e9666358b030" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d1d9cbac-87a6-544e-b307-a6c1f8264aa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-345034" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+8)$ between $x=-2$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{5}{n}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡($\n\n{{field-1}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of subintervals, ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$, and  $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nThe endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=3,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-2)}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(-2+j\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{5}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(-2+\\frac{5j}{n})+8) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{5}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{20j}{n}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8d147c3-255f-563d-8366-a9c38946ae51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385371} {:answer/id #uuid "4bbbf0a4-a602-5069-b4c7-0868f3a3a06f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2i+8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8d147c3-255f-563d-8366-a9c38946ae51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385371} :answer-field/id #uuid "5370c979-ad27-551a-9c6e-df209e21e5f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0cebe607-010c-5dd8-9460-ab5f20c202b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-345037" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{4x+8}$ between $x=-2$ and $x=2$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $8$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $i.$*\n\n${S}_{R}=\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is   \n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n=8$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=2.$ So, the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-(-2)}{8}=\\frac{4}{8}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(-2+i\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}f(-2+\\frac{i}{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}\\,\\sqrt{4\\,(-2+\\frac{i}{2})+8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}\\,\\sqrt{2i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "908d759e-a0ba-5899-b1ce-c908c48106f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8j}{n}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "908d759e-a0ba-5899-b1ce-c908c48106f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8j}{n}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385375} :answer-field/id #uuid "cecd0e6b-5c07-58e7-88f6-555151104bec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d783f47f-8c35-5b8a-93f4-00f2091ffca3" :question/math-academy-id "q-345048" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x-3)$ between $x=1$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{2}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-1}{n}=\\frac{2}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(1+j\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{2}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(1+\\frac{2j}{n})-3)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{2}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1+\\frac{8j}{n}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6af6e813-38f5-5f90-9a13-4a1d0cdbb13c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385378} {:answer/id #uuid "5abeb620-ec17-534d-8c8d-2bff79ba411e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6af6e813-38f5-5f90-9a13-4a1d0cdbb13c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385378} :answer-field/id #uuid "310e936b-18f4-5390-a77f-a9ca3d851ac5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e378236a-5e54-5371-98f4-4839b4a8b16f" :question/math-academy-id "q-345052" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/assets/f321b063e3bc76eeb5b426d00cbf94451a06cec928008eaadc965547691c412a.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=4+x$ between $x=0,$ $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a right Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $i.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=4$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is \n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-0}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(i) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4+i).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f0ac5fe-80cb-52ed-a997-81cd9cce1678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\frac{k}{1+k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385381} {:answer/id #uuid "886fdac8-8fc9-5f50-8dc2-066867d1b2df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=1}^{3}\\frac{1+k}{2+k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385382} {:answer/id #uuid "044aa9f8-5739-5d63-8e2a-ccc771fd4b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\frac{2+k}{1+k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385383} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d837a3-0ff3-5577-b84b-74d77484e0b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=1}^{4}\\frac{2+k}{k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385384} {:answer/id #uuid "c64536d5-100f-5947-ba05-393e8741ac88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=1}^{3}\\frac{3+k}{2+k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "044aa9f8-5739-5d63-8e2a-ccc771fd4b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\frac{2+k}{1+k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385383} :answer-field/id #uuid "b05ab04a-7918-5d9c-99c3-b4fbcfcbfbe3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "adfb3a62-f833-537d-b80b-a21b074c623e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73137" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079618/assets/99f224712b0a067d76bc02c1f33938446ad84883a439ba53cb6569197e2cf9fd.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\frac{x+1}{x}$ between $x=1$, $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-1}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+kΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3-1}f(1+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}f(1+k) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\frac{1+k+1}{1+k} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\frac{2+k}{1+k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35831bb7-3135-595e-bac2-77d7ac80deb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n+4j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385388} {:answer/id #uuid "926011e2-fb23-5d13-850d-2ce4a3204ded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385389} {:answer/id #uuid "59a036d1-1919-570d-ace7-a3c2a521e065" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385390} {:answer/id #uuid "36dffcee-c595-530d-98c2-9b1cae11a9eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n+4j)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385391} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b7dc03-4db0-53f3-a3df-659079fc6c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+4j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36dffcee-c595-530d-98c2-9b1cae11a9eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n+4j)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385391} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b0b6aa0-24a2-5c5c-941f-bc6d23fae870" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eff7f711-e171-56b8-8f66-052602ea7583" :question/math-academy-id "q-73192" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ between $x=1$ and $x=5$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-1}{n}=\\frac{4}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(1+j\\cdot \\frac{4}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(\\frac{n+4j}{n}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{n+4j}{n}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n+4j)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n)].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f0e967-f34a-545d-90f9-8ff010a6763d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\sqrt[n]{{e}^{4j}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385394} {:answer/id #uuid "d7954738-7b7b-5d31-9661-71e5ef06e164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\sqrt[n]{{e}^{j}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385395} {:answer/id #uuid "cebac7df-6382-5df8-a695-dfc2dc2c5042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\sqrt{{e}^{j}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385396} {:answer/id #uuid "376dfc65-32c8-50dd-b889-bbce5e47a3d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\sqrt{{e}^{j}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385397} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd9f3ad-1669-552a-9c68-e1bfa8828832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\sqrt[n]{{e}^{j}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48f0e967-f34a-545d-90f9-8ff010a6763d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\sqrt[n]{{e}^{4j}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385394} :answer-field/id #uuid "85634b0f-049a-5a30-a77e-3fd259d9e250" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fd926104-dccb-5ceb-b205-b99c25d134c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-73208" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y={e}^{x}$ between $x=1$ and $x=5$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is  \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$  with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-1}{n}=\\frac{4}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(1+j\\cdot \\frac{4}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(1+\\frac{4j}{n}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{e}^{(1+\\frac{4j}{n})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{e}^{1}\\cdot {e}^{4j/n} \\\\  & =\\frac{4e}{n}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\sqrt[n]{{e}^{4j}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
